  "relation": "one contract, upstream: GTMisc.X39.x39_separates_xy X Y A and Packing.X26.x26_separates_xy X Y Z (no simple sequence path from X to Y, B5's seq_set_path, has its vertex set, B1's seq_vertices, disjoint from the separator) are transparent aliases of GraphTheory.core.connectivity.separator G X Y A (every packaged Path from a vertex of X to a vertex of Y meets A), with argument order G, X, Y, separator and G implicit as before. GTBase.set_separators.seq_separatorP proves the frozen sequence bodies equivalent without any premise: upstream separatorI reduces arbitrary packaged paths to irredundant ones, whose node lists are set-to-set simple paths (seq_set_path_nodes, seq_vertices_nodes), and every such sequence packages as a Path with the same vertices (Path_of_path, mem_path, nodesE). Nothing restricts X, Y or the separator: endpoints may lie in it, one-vertex paths count, so every common vertex of X and Y lies in it (separator_seq1, upstream separator_cap), and empty endpoint sets are separated by anything. No second predicate, guard or base re-export is introduced. Distinct and untouched: upstream separates x y U, which also requires both endpoints outside U (separator_not_separates), Cycle's multigraph edge separator ueseparates, global vertex cutsets and balanced separators, Digraph dicuts, disjoint path collections and X116's inline hitting clause.",
