  "summary": [
    "B26 set-separator. GTMisc X39 `x39_separates_xy` and Packing X26 `x26_separates_xy` (no simple sequence X-Y path, `seq_set_path`, has its vertex set, `seq_vertices`, disjoint from the separator) are now aliases of upstream `GraphTheory.core.connectivity.separator G X Y A`; argument order and implicit G are unchanged and no guard is added. `GTBase.set_separators.seq_separatorP` proves the frozen bodies equivalent without premises (upstream `separatorI`, `Path_of_path`); the module defines no predicate and is imported explicitly.",
    "",
    "Corners, in the module and the public-only client base/theories/examples/set_separators.v: X, Y and the separator are unrestricted; endpoint hits are allowed; one-vertex paths count (`separator_seq1`); empty endpoint sets and K_0 are separated by anything, the whole carrier separates anything, two edgeless vertices are separated by the empty set, K_2 is cut by either endpoint but not by the empty set; separators are monotone and, in sgraphs, symmetric. Upstream `separates` also requires both endpoints outside U (`separator_not_separates`).",
    "",
    "Rows, frozen exactly and certified by a pointwise separator transport: X39 `coarse_menger_ball_separator_statement`, cross-module X40 `coarse_menger_distance_two_separator_statement` (partial) and X26 `bounded_degree_distant_induced_menger_statement`. B5's complete X39Original, X40Original and X26Original rows (raw B1 support, raw B5 set path and separator; balls still live at this pin) are reused with B5's certificates: six whole iff. Their fourteen frozen pieces are bound as historical objects (B1 9e03072, B5 fbf33a0). The incoming A22 raw-ball Originals are the coordinator's combined-parent obligation; nothing is copied here.",
    "",
    "The fifteen direct B1 / B5 compatibility theorems keep their statements and every frozen body; their proofs move from conversion to `seq_separatorP` and the same transport, and the B1 / B5 specs record this. The reverse-import closure keeps identical old theorem types (vocabulary_packing's thirteen included). Routes: X39 and X40 (graph-theory-misc), X26 (packing-theory); no Digraph source. Baseline a02e1c2 matches the B26 discovery scope byte for byte.",
    "",
    "Private reviewed B26+A22 prerequisite: the initial six whole iff and all older snapshots remain unchanged. Eleven exact A22 mappings add the three complete raw-ball X39/X40/X26 Originals (nine whole iff total), reusing the existing GTMisc/Packing migration.balls original_compat certificates. All four B26-adapted B1/B5 certificate files are retained, so these full proofs compose through the genuine upstream separator bridge. Three partial snapshots in each direction are explicitly recorded; no full history is claimed for a partial snapshot."
  ],
